Z||000003||BellaFiero||08-31-2000||09:22 AM||||Sounds like a pretty good idea... but will the Pontiac logos let light pass through? Or will you use decals? Hey, I was at the El Paso show... I showed up when it died down, I guess, but I still saw some pretty wicked Fieros. Nice interior!! How was that done? Mine was the dark wine colored Fiero, with the Ram-Air Trans AM racing stripes on the hood and the over-the-roof scoops. ( The Subwoofered One ). My girlfriend had a good time, she loves our cars. She wants one too, but the prices around here are ridiculous. If it's junk - $100. But if it remotely runs, seems people think they can get close to $5,000! <BR><P>------------------<BR>"No, no... you can't put that there, it'll be in the way of the Johnson Rod!"  ||||reg||10
Z||000004||mrfixit58||08-31-2000||09:57 AM||||I'm going from memory hear but I think it there is enough space behind the panel so that it can be done. You'll have to modify or make a new emblem because it has a silver metallic backing (that's what gives it it's sparkle)that would block the light. There should be enough room behind it to mount a shallow light housing. You could use something like a side marker housing if it's not too thick and just glue it to the back of the panel. Of course you'd have to cut out the portion of the panel under the existing emblem but that would be simple enough with a drill and file/rasp. Then, just run a wire and splice it into a lighting circuit and -- viola -- ya got nice glowing emblem. It sounds like it would be a neat project. can anyone see why it wouldn't work?<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||286SE'S||08-31-2000||11:14 AM||||For a long life bulb may I recommend one of the new white LED's. They are resistant to shock and have an estimated life of 11 years.<BR>Terry||||reg||7
Z||000006||MikeSchaefer||08-31-2000||11:37 AM||||<B>Bella</B>,  Your car was very very cool!  I love the over the roof scoops.   You have to come back next year, I have a lot more planned now.  That's kind of a weird phenomenon with the pricing, I see it everywhere.<BR>  <B>Mrfixit58</B>,  Do you think I could sand off that metallic backing?  I don't have my emblems on me, I wander what they'll look like without that,  I'll try and sand off the backing on my old pair within this next week and post some pictures.<BR>     <B>286SE'S</B>, Where could I get a pair of those?  Would I be able to wire the white leds in just like a regular light (pos neg).  I would love to use those if they don't require a circuit board or anything.  <BR>    <B>Haze_Performance</B>,  Your car was also beautiful, my girlfriend won't stop talking about it (she is very partial to silver fiero's)<P>Thanks to everyone who posted, I think we might be on to something here.<BR>Michael Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||6
Z||000007||fiero56||08-31-2000||11:47 AM||||<B>SloPonti</B> has done this very thing with the light in the sail panel. I haven't seen him post anything in quite some time, maybe he is away for a little while or just being quiet? He would be able to tell you everything I would think.||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfixit58||08-31-2000||01:42 PM||||Mike,<P>I think the emplems are facited on the back and smooth on the front. If this is the case, you couldn't just sand the silver off. I think it's just paint so you may be able to soak it in oven cleaner and scrub it with a brush to desolve tha paint and leave the plastic unharmed. If you have an old set it would be worth a try.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||BellaFiero||08-31-2000||05:33 PM||||Thanks, Mike!<BR>All right, I'm definitely in with this modification! It would be very cool. I know you can get the sail panel logos from the Fiero Store and what not, does anyone know if those are exactly like factory? Perhaps those would be easier to work with ( i.e. paint or backing not applied ).<P>------------------<BR>"No, no... you can't put that there, it'll be in the way of the Johnson Rod!"  ||||reg||10
Z||000010||Haze_Performance||08-31-2000||09:09 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fiero56:<BR><B>[b]SloPonti</B> has done this very thing with the light in the sail panel. I haven't seen him post anything in quite some time, maybe he is away for a little while or just being quiet? He would be able to tell you everything I would think.[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Mike,<P>This was what I was getting at. He was at the show to. He had the red car with the purple I4 engine. He made his own light up emblems.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>P.S. Thank You.... I liked your car to.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycarsig.jpg">    <B>My 1985 2M4 Sport Coupe </B><P><BR><B>My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A></B><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 08-31-2000).]||||reg||14
