Z||000013||theogre||09-01-2000||01:07 PM||||The LED is available thru most electronics parts houses. You don't need a circuit board but you do need a resistor to limit current. The resistor depends on the specific LED so I can't give you the value of it.<P>You'd need to solder the resistor and wires to the LED. Then you could put shrink tube on the leads to prevent a short. Just slide a peice of shrink over the whole resistor and the lead it's connected to.||||reg||1
